WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.355
Light can read molecules.

2
00:00:02.455 --> 00:00:04.538
And chemistry is everywhere you look.

3
00:00:09.799 --> 00:00:17.934
In NMR, a strong magnet makes every hydrogen nucleus sing at its own radio frequency, depending on its neighbours.

4
00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:27.617
Ethanol gives three signals in a three, two, one ratio, one for each kind of hydrogen. A stronger magnet spreads them further apart.

5
00:00:28.317 --> 00:00:37.380
Now solve one. A mystery spectrum, formula C₂H₆O. A triplet and a quartet mean an ethyl group, so it must be ethanol.

6
00:00:38.179 --> 00:00:48.534
Infrared light makes bonds vibrate. Each bond absorbs its own frequency, so acetone's C=O double bond shows up as one deep dip.

7
00:00:49.334 --> 00:00:57.340
Visible light tells a colour story. The longer a chain of alternating double bonds, the longer the wavelength it absorbs.

8
00:00:57.739 --> 00:01:05.381
At eleven, that's β-carotene. It soaks up blue light, so what's left looks orange. That's why carrots are orange.

9
00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:14.012
Chromatography races a mixture across a plate. Polar dyes stick and lag behind, so one dot splits into bands.

10
00:01:14.813 --> 00:01:24.382
Your phone battery shuttles lithium ions. As you use it, they leave the graphite for cobalt oxide, while electrons power your phone through the wire.

11
00:01:24.981 --> 00:01:28.111
Charging pushes them all back, ready for tomorrow.

12
00:01:28.911 --> 00:01:36.626
Heat a metal, and its electrons jump up, then fall back, giving off light of exact colours. Sodium glows yellow.

13
00:01:37.326 --> 00:01:43.833
A mystery flame: deep crimson, with bright red lines. It's strontium, the colour of red fireworks.

14
00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:53.929
Inside every cell, thousands of reactions link up like a subway map. Glucose is split in glycolysis, then burned in the Krebs cycle.

15
00:01:54.528 --> 00:02:01.326
The electrons stripped away make ATP: the energy currency behind every heartbeat, and every thought.

16
00:02:04.833 --> 00:02:07.521
Light reveals what molecules are made of.

17
00:02:07.621 --> 00:02:10.187
Colour comes from electrons absorbing light.

18
00:02:10.287 --> 00:02:12.965
And chemistry runs your phone and your cells.

19
00:02:14.233 --> 00:02:16.477
Thanks for watching Quantum Playground.
